    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-ăcerbus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very harsh</i> to the taste. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uva peracerba gustatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 15, 53</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>very painful</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mihi peracerbum fuit, quod, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 6, 5, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
